## Errors & Mistakes
- First probe used a bat-and-ball puzzle; too trivial, adaptive thinking never fired, which made the additional_drop_params: [thinking] look like the culprit. It was not. Use the prime-sum prompt ("sum of all primes between 100 and 200") to make Claude think.
- Assumed reasoning_effort in litellm_params would just work; on 1.99.0 and 1.100.0 it is silently dropped on the chat route (see Codebase Discoveries).
- Used reasoning_effort: bogus as a forwarding probe for gpt-6-astra. Invalid for the chat-to-Responses bridge: LiteLLM drops unknown values before mapping, so a 200 proves nothing there. Use none/minimal instead; Copilot's Responses endpoint rejects them for gpt-6-astra with "Unsupported value", which proves the param arrived.
- litellm.aresponses(model="github_copilot/gpt-6-astra") in the SDK without register_model({...mode: responses}) falls back to chat/completions and Copilot returns 'model "gpt-6-astra" is not accessible via the /chat/completions endpoint'.
- One curl+jq pipeline printed nothing for gpt-6-astra; it was my jq filter, not the proxy.

