## Hints for Future Agents
- Config changes need `litellm-proxy.sh restart`; the container is recreated, so anything docker cp'd into it is gone.
- LiteLLM router merges request kwargs OVER litellm_params, but reasoning_effort in litellm_params still wins over a request-level thinking param on /v1/messages (thinking: disabled and legacy budget_tokens both still ran at the configured effort). Only a request output_config.effort overrides it. Clients cannot turn thinking off once the default is set.
- Copilot accepts low/medium/high/xhigh/max for both models. GPT-6 Astra rejects none and minimal. Copilot default with no params: claude-fable-5 thinks, claude-fable-5.1 does not.
- additional_drop_params: [thinking] on the other four Claude entries is dead config on 1.100.0: no effect on /v1/messages (LiteLLM converts the legacy thinking shape to adaptive and forwards it), and the chat route drops thinking anyway. Not removed because out of scope; candidate for deletion.
- Copilot chat/completions for Claude does not return thinking text; the only signal is completion_tokens jumping (about 5 text + about 200 thinking at high).
- Copilot's /models also lists claude-opus-5 and claude-sonnet-5, not yet in config.

## Codebase Discoveries
- Root cause of the drop: GithubCopilotConfig (litellm/llms/github_copilot/chat/transformation.py) overrides get_supported_openai_params to add thinking and reasoning_effort for Claude, but inherits map_openai_params from litellm/llms/openai/openai.py, which delegates to litellm.openAIGPTConfig.map_openai_params, a separate OpenAIGPTConfig instance that consults ITS OWN supported list. So the override is never used. Independent of drop_params (verified with drop_params=False). gpt-6-astra hits the same filter for a second reason: name matches neither is_model_gpt_5_model nor the model map.
- allowed_openai_params: [reasoning_effort] in litellm_params bypasses that filter on both the Claude chat route and the gpt chat-to-Responses bridge. Verified on the wire via SDK and via proxy (bogus -> Copilot 400 for claude-fable-5.1; none -> Copilot 400 for gpt-6-astra).
- /v1/messages route (GithubCopilotAnthropicMessagesConfig) translates reasoning_effort into thinking: {type: adaptive, display: summarized} + output_config: {effort: X}, and converts legacy budget_tokens into adaptive + effort (1024 -> low, 4096 -> high).
- renovate.json still has a stale regex manager for LITELLM_VERSION in litellm-proxy.sh; that variable no longer exists. The digest bumps come from the built-in docker-compose manager.
- The post-commit hook autopushes master to origin immediately.

